  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CENTRALASIENGRUPPERNA (CSO-STRATEGIN 2025-2029)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Asia Solidarity Group CSO Strategy 2025-2029 - Central Asia Solidarity Group CSO Strategy 2025-28</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Centralasiengrupperna (CAG) samarbetar inom programmet med fyra partners i tre l&#xe4;nder; Kirgizistan, Uzbekistan samt Tadzjikistan. Projektet har flera &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttningar; att motverka det krympande utrymmet f&#xf6;r civila samh&#xe4;llet i regionen, st&#xe4;rka resiliensen mot klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar, st&#xe4;rka kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter samt motverka k&#xf6;nsbaserat v&#xe5;ld. Varje samarbetsorganisation arbetar f&#xf6;r att l&#xf6;sa sina egna identifierade problem och samarbetet fokuserar d&#xe4;rf&#xf6;r p&#xe5; respektive organisations unika kontext och syfte. Insatsen &#xe4;r inriktad p&#xe5; kunskaps&#xf6;verf&#xf6;ring, utbildningar, dialog och deltagande och utformas i n&#xe4;ra samarbete mellan CAG och den lokala partnern.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Central Asia Groups (CAG) collaborate within the programme with four partners in three countries: Kyrgyzstan, Uzbekistan and Tajikistan. The project has several overarching objectives: to counteract the shrinking space for civil society in the region, strengthen resilience to climate change, strengthen women&apos;s rights and combat gender-based violence. Each partnerorganisation works to solve its own identified problems, and the collaboration therefore focuses on each organisation&apos;s unique context and purpose. The initiative focuses on knowledge transfer, training, dialogue and participation, and is designed in close collaboration between CAG and the local partner.</narrative>
  </description>
